WEBVTT

00:05:29.082 --> 00:05:31.750
the idea is that one
country's nuclear weapons

00:05:31.774 --> 00:05:34.761
prevents another country
from using theirs.

00:05:34.785 --> 00:05:38.511
So you nuke me, I nuke you,

00:05:38.535 --> 00:05:39.828
and we both lose.

00:05:40.794 --> 00:05:43.474
So in a way, there's a stalemate.

00:05:43.498 --> 00:05:46.028
No one uses their weapons,
and we're all safe.

00:05:47.487 --> 00:05:52.686
But this theory has real questions.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:55.511
There are experts
who challenge this theory

00:05:55.535 --> 00:05:58.662
and wonder: Does it really work
this way in practice?

00:05:59.516 --> 00:06:04.492
It certainly doesn't allow
for mistakes or miscalculations.